## 18:25–19:30 — What science can and cannot add

### Writer instruction

Use death psychology cautiously.

Documented findings:

* reminders of death can increase defensiveness, worldview protection and in-group attachment;
* results vary substantially;
* recent reviews identify publication-bias and replication concerns;
* structured death reflection may differ from a sudden mortality reminder;
* one recent controlled art-based death meditation increased connectedness and appreciation of life, but that does not establish the effects of cremation-ground practice. ([PubMed][5])

Best conclusion:

> Exposure to death does not automatically dissolve ego. Unstructured exposure may strengthen it. The tantric hypothesis was that ritual framing, metaphysics, initiation and attention could transform the response.

